{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeFullTwistProduct","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeFullTwistProduct","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeTranspositionExpansion"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmProd_three_eq_fullTwist3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmProd_three_eq_fullTwist3","kind":"theorem","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeFullTwistProduct.lean#L280-L286","doc":"The `n = 3` case of `HeckeJucysMurphyElements.jmRaw_prod_three`, recovered from the general\ntheorem — the hand proof there used one explicit braid move on a six-letter word; this one is the\n`n = 2` instance of an induction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmProd_two_eq_fullTwist2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmProd_two_eq_fullTwist2","kind":"theorem","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeFullTwistProduct.lean#L273-L278","doc":"The `n = 2` case of `HeckeJucysMurphyElements.jmRaw_prod_two`, recovered from the general\ntheorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.delta_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.delta_two","kind":"theorem","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeFullTwistProduct.lean#L270-L271","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmProd_eq_delta_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmProd_eq_delta_pow","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeFullTwistProduct.lean#L253-L266","doc":"**`∏Lᵢ = Δ²`, for every `n`.**  `L₀L₁⋯Lₙ = (delta n)^{n+1}`, the full twist of `B_{n+1}`.\n\nProved from the braid relations alone — the Hecke relation is not used anywhere in this file, and\nneither is `jmRaw_comm` (which makes the product order-independent, a different statement). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmProd_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmProd_succ","kind":"theorem","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeFullTwistProduct.lean#L250-L251","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmProd","kind":"def","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeFullTwistProduct.lean#L244-L248","doc":"The ordered product `L₀ L₁ ⋯ L_{n−1}`.  A `Finset.prod` is unavailable here — `A` is not\ncommutative — so the product is defined by its own recursion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_eq_run_mul_delta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_eq_run_mul_delta","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeFullTwistProduct.lean#L233-L242","doc":"**The JM element as a word**: `Lₖ = run 0 k · delta k`, i.e. `σ_{k−1}⋯σ₀ · σ₀⋯σ_{k−1}`.  This is\njust its own recursion read as a word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.delta_twist_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.delta_twist_step","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeFullTwistProduct.lean#L226-L231","doc":"**The twist step**: `(delta (n+1))^{n+1} = (delta n)^{n+1} · run 0 (n+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.delta_pow_run","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.delta_pow_run","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeFullTwistProduct.lean#L204-L224","doc":"**The engine**: `(delta m · σ_m)^{k+1} = (delta m)^{k+1} · run b (k+1)` for `m = b + k`.\n\nThe free bottom index `b` is load-bearing — the inductive step consumes the hypothesis at `b+1`, so\na version stated only at `b = 0` does not close. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.run_push","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.run_push","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeFullTwistProduct.lean#L145-L200","doc":"**The push law** — the only place a braid move happens in this file.\n\n    run (b+1) j · delta m · σ_m  =  delta m · run (b+1) j · σ_b        (m = b + j)\n\nA descending run can be carried through `delta`; the price is that the trailing generator drops from\n`σ_m` all the way to `σ_b`.  That drop is exactly what turns the ascending-run power into a JM\nelement in `delta_pow_run`.\n\nThe index `m` is carried as a variable with `m = b + j` as a hypothesis rather than written as\n`b + j` inline: the induction re-associates the sum at every step, and a syntactic `b + j` would\nforce a rewrite before each use. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.core_braid_push","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.core_braid_push","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeFullTwistProduct.lean#L122-L143","doc":"**The push law's core braid step**, isolated.\n\nFor any `r` commuting with `σ_{m+1}`, and any `b < m`:\n\n    σ_{m+1} · (σ_m r) · σ_b · σ_{m+1}  =  σ_m · (σ_{m+1} · (σ_m r)) · σ_b\n\n`σ_b` slides past `σ_{m+1}` (they are `≥ 2` apart because `b < m`), `σ_{m+1}` slides past `r` by\nhypothesis, and what is left is the braid relation on `σ_m, σ_{m+1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_delta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_delta","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeFullTwistProduct.lean#L104-L120","doc":"`σ_j` commutes with `delta m` whenever `m < j` — every letter of `delta m` has index `≤ m−1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_run","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_run","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeFullTwistProduct.lean#L86-L102","doc":"`σ_j` commutes with a whole descending run whose letters all sit at distance `≥ 2` below `j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.run_peel_bot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.run_peel_bot","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeFullTwistProduct.lean#L75-L84","doc":"The same run peeled from the **bottom** instead: `run b (k+1) = run (b+1) k · σ_b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.run_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.run_succ","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeFullTwistProduct.lean#L72-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.run_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.run_zero","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeFullTwistProduct.lean#L70-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.delta_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.delta_succ","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeFullTwistProduct.lean#L67-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.delta_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.delta_zero","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeFullTwistProduct.lean#L65-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.run","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.run","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeFullTwistProduct.lean#L59-L63","doc":"**Descending run** `run b k = σ_{b+k−1} σ_{b+k−2} ⋯ σ_b`, peeled from the top so that the\nbottom index `b` stays fixed under the recursion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.delta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.delta","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeFullTwistProduct.lean#L53-L57","doc":"**Ascending run** `delta k = σ₀ σ₁ ⋯ σ_{k−1}`.  The full twist of `B_{n+1}` is\n`(delta n)^{n+1}`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}